\ rest ( var -- pattern ): wrap a logic variable or _ so that, as the last
\ element of an array pattern, it takes the remaining elements of the other
\ side as a fresh array under unify. Prefix elements unify pairwise; a subject
\ shorter than the prefix is a mismatch, not an error.

\ === binding the head and the rest ===
lvar to Hd  lvar to Tl
[ 1 2 3 4 ] [ Hd Tl rest ] ~ drop  Hd ? . Tl ? . cr      \ 1 [ 2 3 4 ]
lvar to Only
[ 7 ] [ _ Only rest ] ~ drop  Only ? . cr               \ [ ]  (the rest of a one-element array is empty)
lvar to Whole
[ 5 6 ] [ Whole rest ] ~ drop  Whole ? . cr             \ [ 5 6 ]  (a bare rest takes everything)

\ === the wildcard rest ignores the remainder ===
[ 1 2 ] [ _ rest ] matches? .  [ ] [ _ rest ] matches? .  [ ] [ _ _ rest ] matches? . cr   \ 1 1 0  (a bare wildcard rest takes an empty remainder too)

\ === nested, and inside a frame value ===
lvar to Inner
[ [ 1 2 3 ] 9 ] [ [ _ Inner rest ] _ ] ~ drop  Inner ? . cr   \ [ 2 3 ]
lvar to Args
{ :cmd :run :args [ :x 1 2 ] } { :args [ _ Args rest ] } ~ drop  Args ? . cr   \ [ 1 2 ]

\ === case/of dispatches by shape ===
: shape case [ ] of "empty" endof [ _ ] of "one" endof [ _ _ rest ] of "two or more" endof drop "not an array" endcase . cr ;
[ ] shape [ 5 ] shape [ 5 6 7 ] shape 42 shape           \ empty / one / two or more / not an array

\ === a fresh rest variable per call via a ?-local ===
: tail-of | ?tail-var | [ _ tail-var rest ] ~ drop tail-var ? ;
[ 1 2 3 ] tail-of . [ 1 ] tail-of . cr                  \ [ 2 3 ] [ ]

\ === a bound rest variable compares structurally on the next use ===
lvar to Bound
[ 1 2 ] [ Bound rest ] ~ drop
[ 5 6 ] [ Bound rest ] matches? . [ 1 2 ] [ Bound rest ] matches? . cr   \ 0 1

\ === printing, type, copy ===
[ Hd Tl rest ] . cr                                     \ [ Hd=1 ..Tl=[ 2 3 4 ] ]
lvar rest . _ rest . cr                                 \ .._N .._
lvar rest type-of . cr                                  \ :rest
lvar to Orig
[ _ Orig rest ] copy [ 1 2 3 ] ~ drop  Orig ? . cr       \ ?Orig  (the copy carries a fresh variable)

\ === the binding survives a collection ===
lvar to Kept
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] [ _ Kept rest ] ~ drop gc Kept ? . cr      \ [ 2 3 4 5 ]

clear

\ === errors ===
5 rest                                                  \ (rest takes a logic variable or _)
[ lvar rest 1 ] [ 1 2 ] ~                               \ (rest must be last)
[ lvar rest ] [ lvar rest ] ~                           \ (two rest patterns)
lvar rest value>bytes                                   \ (not serializable)
